# Round XXIX Track A: `t[5]` on a `Tuple` REJECTS at check-time with
# `E_NotIndexable`. Tuples use the dot-N accessor `t.0`, `t.1`, etc. —
# not the `[]` operator (D39; there is no dynamic-index-into-tuple
# semantics today, so `Tuple` implements no `Index` impl).
#
# Pre-fix: silent-accept + unchecked offset read.
# Post-fix: rejects with E_NotIndexable — `ResolvedType::Tuple` has no
# registry key (`type_key_for_trait_lookup` returns `None`), the
# `Expr::Index` arm's anonymous-type branch describes it and rejects.
int main():
    (int, int) t = (10, 20)
    int x = t[5]
    print(x)
    return 0
